1
00:00:03,371 --> 00:00:06,174
50 years have passed,

2
00:00:06,207 --> 00:00:11,045
but I do not age.

3
00:00:11,079 --> 00:00:17,185
Time has lost its effect on me.

4
00:00:21,089 --> 00:00:24,858
Yet the suffering
continues.

5
00:00:26,394 --> 00:00:28,896
Aku's grasp chokes the past,

6
00:00:28,929 --> 00:00:32,533
present, and future.

7
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:36,437
Hope is lost.

8
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,572
Gotta get back,

9
00:00:38,606 --> 00:00:40,608
back to the past.

10
00:00:40,641 --> 00:00:42,743
Samurai Jack.

11
00:01:30,424 --> 00:01:35,028
Master, new arrivals
have come to offer tribute!

12
00:01:38,699 --> 00:01:42,069
Oh, great Shogun of Sorrow,

13
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:44,905
Master of All Masters,

14
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:48,108
you have allowed us
to inhabit this world,

15
00:01:48,142 --> 00:01:51,312
and for that,
we are forever grateful.

16
00:01:52,646 --> 00:01:55,316
We offer you
a special tribute.

17
00:01:55,349 --> 00:01:56,650
Stop!

18
00:01:56,684 --> 00:01:59,153
Look at what you're doing!

19
00:01:59,187 --> 00:02:03,123
You're getting yourselves
all over the floor.

20
00:02:03,157 --> 00:02:04,091
Uh...

21
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:07,328
I just had it vacuumed.

22
00:02:07,361 --> 00:02:09,129
Out. Out!

23
00:02:09,163 --> 00:02:11,031
Get out!

24
00:02:11,064 --> 00:02:16,304
Master,
Master, we've done it.

25
00:02:16,337 --> 00:02:18,105
May I introduce

26
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:22,376
the most epic version
of the beetle drone yet!

27
00:02:25,012 --> 00:02:27,114
And I care because?

28
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:29,350
B-B-Because
the Samurai.

29
00:02:29,383 --> 00:02:31,051
You've wanted to kill him
since forever.

30
00:02:31,084 --> 00:02:33,554
He's the bane
of your existence.

31
00:02:33,587 --> 00:02:34,888
Oh!

32
00:02:34,922 --> 00:02:38,526
That was the old Aku.

33
00:02:38,559 --> 00:02:41,028
This is the new Aku.

34
00:02:41,061 --> 00:02:45,833
And he really doesn't care
about a pathetic samurai

35
00:02:45,866 --> 00:02:48,836
who wanders around
like a mad fool.

36
00:02:48,869 --> 00:02:50,037
Ha!

37
00:02:50,070 --> 00:02:52,573
It's hilarious, really.

38
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:55,676
Look, I tell you what --

39
00:02:55,709 --> 00:02:59,647
you want to destroy him,
go ahead.

40
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,749
Who cares?

41
00:03:01,782 --> 00:03:07,888
I certainly don't,
not one bit at all.

42
00:03:13,294 --> 00:03:17,030
So, tell me
what's been bothering you.

43
00:03:17,064 --> 00:03:19,400
Well, you see, Doc,

44
00:03:19,433 --> 00:03:22,836
it's been
over 50 years already.

45
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:24,738
It's been that long?

46
00:03:24,772 --> 00:03:26,039
Yes.

47
00:03:26,073 --> 00:03:28,842
You see,
that's the actual problem.

48
00:03:28,876 --> 00:03:32,613
Once I eradicated

49
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:34,382
all the time portals,

50
00:03:34,415 --> 00:03:38,185
I thought I would just wait it
out and then the Samur--

51
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,421
We don't
say his name here.

52
00:03:40,454 --> 00:03:43,090
It is a safe place.

53
00:03:43,123 --> 00:03:46,093
Yes.
Sorry, Doctor.

54
00:03:46,126 --> 00:03:49,062
Well, I-I just assumed
that eventually

55
00:03:49,096 --> 00:03:51,765
over time he would just

56
00:03:51,799 --> 00:03:56,069
Di-i-i-i-e! di-i-i-i-e!

57
00:03:56,103 --> 00:04:00,040
But he hasn't even aged.

58
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:02,142
I mean, like, at all.

59
00:04:02,175 --> 00:04:04,978
He just grew
that stupid beard.

60
00:04:05,012 --> 00:04:08,482
It looks like
he'll be here forever!

61
00:04:08,516 --> 00:04:14,422
I-I just don't know
if I can handle that.

62
00:04:14,455 --> 00:04:18,426
Yes. It seems that
the initial time travel

63
00:04:18,459 --> 00:04:22,296
has affected
the aging process.

64
00:04:22,330 --> 00:04:25,333
It's quite
the conundrum.

65
00:04:25,366 --> 00:04:27,134
Yes.

66
00:04:27,167 --> 00:04:29,437
What is that again?

67
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:34,007
Just a confusing
or difficult problem.

68
00:04:34,041 --> 00:04:37,244
Yes. Problem.

69
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:42,115
I wish there was someone who
can dispose of my problem.

70
00:04:42,149 --> 00:04:47,921
Yes. One can hope.
Yes. One can hope.

71
00:08:57,771 --> 00:08:59,740
Ahh!

72
00:09:49,522 --> 00:09:52,092
It's time to end it,
don't you think?

73
00:09:52,125 --> 00:09:55,062
Never.
They are just machines.

74
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:56,930
I'll find a way.
I always have.

75
00:09:56,964 --> 00:09:59,800
When you have the sword,
but now it's gone.

76
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:01,401
There's no hope!

77
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:03,303
I've been doing fine
without it.

78
00:10:03,336 --> 00:10:04,905
Well, listen to you.

79
00:10:04,938 --> 00:10:07,174
And what are you going to do
when Aku finds you

80
00:10:07,207 --> 00:10:08,976
and realizes
you have no sword?

81
00:10:09,009 --> 00:10:12,746
Aku doesn't know, and he hasn't
shown himself in years.

82
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:16,483
He keeps thinking that one of
his machines can defeat me.

83
00:10:16,516 --> 00:10:18,151
Maybe he's right.

84
00:10:18,185 --> 00:10:20,353
You haven't faced anything
so powerful.

85
00:10:20,387 --> 00:10:22,489
How much longer
can you keep this up?

86
00:10:22,522 --> 00:10:26,093
It always seems bad at first,
but then I find a way.

87
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:28,195
They're just
nuts and bolts,

88
00:10:28,228 --> 00:10:30,831
just nuts and bolts.

89
00:10:30,864 --> 00:10:32,265
Who cares anymore?!

90
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:33,433
There's no way home.

91
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:35,168
There's nothing
to fight for.

92
00:10:35,202 --> 00:10:37,170
There's no more honor.

93
00:10:37,204 --> 00:10:38,806
Come to think of it,

94
00:10:38,839 --> 00:10:41,341
the only honorable thing
to do is --

95
00:10:41,374 --> 00:10:42,943
Quiet.
No!

96
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:46,880
I won't spend eternity
in this forsaken time!

97
00:10:46,914 --> 00:10:49,482
What do you want from me?

98
00:10:49,516 --> 00:10:52,319
I want it to end.

99
00:10:52,352 --> 00:10:54,054
Aren't you tired?

100
00:10:54,087 --> 00:10:57,858
Wouldn't it be great to be free
of all of this?

101
00:10:57,891 --> 00:11:00,961
Our ancestors
are waiting for us.

102
00:11:00,994 --> 00:11:03,897
They want you
to join them.

103
00:11:11,238 --> 00:11:13,040
There.
You'll never make it!

104
00:11:13,073 --> 00:11:14,141
They'll get you!

105
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:15,442
I'll make it.

106
00:19:18,191 --> 00:19:20,360
Ahh!

107
00:21:53,012 --> 00:21:54,647
* Watch out
* Gotta get back

108
00:21:54,681 --> 00:21:56,349
* Back to the past
* Samurai Jack

109
00:21:56,383 --> 00:21:58,418
* Jack, Jack, Jack, Jack, Jack
* Wa-Watch out

110
00:22:04,424 --> 00:22:05,992
* Gotta get back,
back to the past, Samurai Jack *

111
00:22:06,025 --> 00:22:10,229
* Watch out

112
00:22:10,262 --> 00:22:15,468
* Jack, Jack, Jack, Jack, Jack

113
00:22:15,502 --> 00:22:17,003
* Watch out

114
00:22:17,036 --> 00:22:18,137
* Gotta get back

115
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:19,138
* Jack, Jack, Jack

116
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:20,673
* Samurai Jack

117
00:22:20,707 --> 00:22:24,276
* Jack, Jack, Jack, Jack, Jack
* Wa-Watch out
